    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### **Implementing Weighted Rating System (Structuring & Enriching)**\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CCw2tONMx0AP"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### **Filtering (Structuring)**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JmEwM7JxyM7R"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We choose a threshold of 100 votes which is slightly above the median (77.5) while far below the maximum (38,276), ensuring ratings are based on a reasonably large sample without excluding most films."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "t9JBXBza70O9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df_TMDB = TMDB_filtered.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "qualified = df_TMDB[df_TMDB[\"vote_count\"] >= 100].copy()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Auzd56jbyWNR"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### **Feature Engineering (Enriching)**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kI8s4lwXSqcD"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We introduced a **weighted rating system** to make movie ratings more fair and reliable as the number of votes differs greatly across movies. Some movies may have very high average ratings, but these ratings are based on only a smaller number of reviews, making them less representative of general audience opinion. If we relied only on the raw vote average, such movies could appear misleadingly stronger as compared to movies that were rated by many more viewers.\n",
        "\n",
        "To account for this, we adjusted each movie’s rating by considering both its average score and its number of votes. This allows movies with very few votes to have their ratings pulled closer to the overall average rating of all movies, reducing the effect of small-sample bias. On the other hand, movies with a large number of votes retain ratings that are closer to their observed average, since they are supported by more reliable evidence. In our formula, 100 is the minimum vote threshold set earlier, meaning a movie must have at least 100 votes for its own rating to carry stronger weight in the weighted score.\n",
        "\n",
        "We used the following formula: ![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ac5W0yRTFOFI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "C = df_TMDB[\"vote_average\"].mean()\n",
        "m = 100\n",
        "\n",
        "def weighted_rating(x, m=m, C=C):\n",
        "    v = x[\"vote_count\"]\n",
        "    R = x[\"vote_average\"]\n",
        "    return (v / (v + m) * R) + (m / (v + m) * C)\n",
        "\n",
        "qualified[\"weighted_rating\"] = qualified.apply(weighted_rating, axis=1)\n",
        "qualified = qualified.sort_values(\"weighted_rating\", ascending=False)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ib2cLGD_ShEj"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
