      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "###<font color = #68b383>**Step 1: Raw Revenue Analysis**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** To examine whether releasing a film within ±7 days of a major studio film is associated with lower box office revenue.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Method/Measure:** Films are split into 2 groups based on the faced_major_studio boolean variable - those that were released within ±7 days of a Big Six studio film, and those that did not. We first conducted a raw revenue comparison of the median and mean worldwide box office revenues across the 2 groups.  \n",
        "\n",
        "Results were then visualised using a box plot to compare the spread, as well as a log-scale histogram for distributional shape. A log transformation was applied to revenue for the histogram as box office revenue is heavily right-skewed (a small number of blockbusters earn billions while most films earn far less). The log-scale spreads the distribution evenly, allowing meaningful visual comparison between the two groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "Lastly, a subgroup breakdown further separated each group into major studio films and non-major (indie) films for comparision.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Code:** Raw revenue comparison of median and mean. For each group, we generate a boxplot. We will also plot a log Revenue distribution histogram.\n",
        "\n",
        "Both measure of central tendency (median and mean) and measure of dispersion (interquartile range via box plot, distributional spread via log-scale histogram) were used to compare box office revenue across the groups.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CW7DkQVHWdV6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#Filter Dataframe into 2 groups, films that faced major studio and those that did not\n",
