        "Therefore, we use the subgroup breakdown for a more meaningful comparison. Major studio films earn a median of 174.0 Million when facing a major competitor compared to 197.7 Million in the Safe Window^. This suggests that  major studio films experience a reduction in revenue from direct competition with other major studios.\n",
        "\n",
        "Interestingly, non-major (indie) films show the opposite pattern. They earn a marginally higher median when facing a major studio (103.0 Million) versus a safe window (100.9 Million). This is counterintuitive but may be explained by the fact that major studio blockbusters tend to release during peak cinema periods like the holidays, driving higher overall audience footfall that benefits all films releasing in the same window, including indie films.\n",
