        "####<font color = #68b383>**Hypothesis Testing**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** To determine if there is a statistically significant difference in median revenue between movies that faced major studio competition (Competed) and those that did not (Safe). By segmenting the data into quality tiers and studio types, our aim is to see if specific type of films are more vulnerable when released alongside movies from major studio.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Method/Measure:** We use hypothesis testing, specifically the Mann-Whitney U test. It is a non-parametric test used to compare medians of 2 independent group. Since box office revenue is heavily skewed and contain signficant outliers, we choose this test over T-test as it handles non-normal distribution by looking at ranks. To ensure fairness, the data is binned by weighted_rating, ensuring that we are comparing movies of similar movie rating.\n",
        "\n",
        "Our Null-hypothesis is that there is no difference between median revenue between movies that faced major studio competition and those that did not. The alternative hyothesis is that there is a significant difference.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Code:** We first plot the distribution for box office revenue to illustrate the right-skewness as mentioned previously. We will use this to determine which statistical test to use. The second part performs the Mann-Whitney U Test to compare medians of movies in the safe window and movies who have competition.  \n"
      ],
